a new independent poll breaking clearly for either candidate could move this off the knife's edge.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Bill Huizenga (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Southwest Michigan's 4th District is one of the closest House races of 2026. Incumbent Bill Huizenga, a Republican seeking another term, faces Democratic state senator Sean McCann in a district with a modest Republican lean but a strongly favorable Democratic national environment. Huizenga has out-raised McCann and holds a cash advantage, though outside groups have spent heavily against him while McCann has drawn support from groups like GIFFORDS PAC.\n\nExpert ratings are split: several rate the race Lean R, while Sabato's Crystal Ball, Silver Bulletin, Split Ticket, The Economist, and Fox News call it a Tossup, and one rates it Lean D. A September GBAO poll showed McCann up one point, and prediction markets price Huizenga's chances only slightly above even. The race sits right at the tipping point.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5309, "margin": 0.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4711, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4732, "margin": -1.0}]}